 "text": "Hey there, how are you feeling? A sketch is short and funny, usually just one scene or idea, while a study is longer and takes a character's story seriously. Kind of, yes. It' the short version of writing a play from rough idea to finished script. Lovely. Start with the big idea, and build from there. Clouds look like anything, from kittens to giant water balloons. Does it matter what they look like, or how you use them? The big idea, and how it changes the landscape. If you start with the clouds, you might get stuck there. Good idea. Roughly how big is your landscape?",
